      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "p3-1-1",
          "panel": 1,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "主人が始めました。今年で、最後にしようと",
          "en": "My husband started it. I want this year to be the last."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-2-1",
          "panel": 2,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "予約は百人。でも、着る着物と、着せる手が足りません",
          "en": "A hundred signed up. But we're short on kimono and on dressers."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-2-2",
          "panel": 2,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "タンスにあるのは、どのくらい？",
          "en": "How many are in your chests?"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-2-3",
          "panel": 2,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "預かったものが、二百枚ほど",
          "en": "About two hundred, held in trust."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-2-4",
          "panel": 2,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "パレードで着てもらう約束で、お預かりしたものです",
          "en": "Lent to us on the promise they'd be worn in the parade."
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-3-1",
          "panel": 3,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "着付けって、帯をぐるぐる回すやつですよね？",
          "en": "Kimono dressing... that's spinning the sash around, right?",
          "note": "Kitsuke (kimono dressing) is a skill of its own: layers, cords and the obi sash go on in a set order, and many people hire a dresser for formal occasions."
        }
      ]
    },
