      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "p5-1-1",
          "panel": 1,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "まず、肌着と足袋。それから長襦袢",
          "en": "First, underwear and tabi socks. Then the under-kimono."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-2-1",
          "panel": 2,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "衿は、首の後ろをこぶし一つ分、抜きます",
          "en": "Pull the collar back from the nape, one fist's width."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-3-1",
          "panel": 3,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "右を先に、左を上に。右前です",
          "en": "Right side first, left on top. That's \"right-front.\"",
          "note": "\"Right-front\" (migi-mae) means the right panel goes on first, under the left. Everyone, men and women, wears kimono this way."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-4-1",
          "panel": 4,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "右前……",
          "en": "Right-front..."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-5-1",
          "panel": 5,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "右手が、懐に入る形",
          "en": "So your right hand can slip inside."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-6-1",
          "panel": 6,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "おお～、赤嶺が着物……",
          "en": "Ooh, Akamine in a kimono..."
        },
        {
          "id": "p5-6-2",
          "panel": 6,
          "type": "speech",
          "ja": "のぞくな!!",
          "en": "NO PEEKING!!"
        }
      ]
    },
